{"name":"Homoeopathic Blue","hex":"#dbe7e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"homoeopathic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of homeopathic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homoeopathic"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Homeopathy","blocks":[{"text":"Homeopathy or homoeopathy is a pseudoscientific system of alternative medicine. It was conceived in 1796 by the German physician Samuel Hahnemann. Its practitioners, called homeopaths or homeopathic physicians, believe that a substance that causes symptoms of a disease in healthy people can cure similar symptoms in sick people; this doctrine is called similia similibus curentur, or \"like cures like\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg/330px-Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeopathy","wikidata":"Q81058"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/1280px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeopathy-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/1280px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Samuel Hahnemann Monument, Washington, D.C., with the inscription Similia Similibus Curentur – \"Like cures Like\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASamuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or